A stall that was not on this path yesterday squats on the dry hump ahead, tended by something that is mostly hat and grin. Pollen-Factor Dree Honeythief, licensed by nobody, trusted by fewer.
pollen_factor_dree: Fresh blessings! Each one hand-picked, each one deeply grateful to be sold! No coin? No matter. This one's already decided. It's a gift. Gifts are binding.
pollen_factor_dree: Take it, take it. It wants to be taken. That's the curse, technically. It's lonely. It will fix that. It will fix that with you.
pollen_factor_dree: Cursed, yes, openly, on the label — I'm not the Pale Court, I disclose. Powerful, though. The curse is why it's powerful. They usually are.
[Something small and wrapped and faintly warm is in your pack now. You do not remember agreeing to this. Dree is already folding the stall.]
pollen_factor_dree: Non-refundable. Also it screams at night. Enjoy!
